        "PMC7012927::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic Al–Co–Cr–Fe–Ni is a predominantly disordered, single-phase FCC solid solution without substantive ordering.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing Al raises the chemical driving force for ordering.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11396108::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The increased ordering drive facilitates nucleation of γ′ within the high-entropy matrix.",
